# Security

## Card & PII

- Never log PAN, CVV, full card, or raw provider private keys (use shared logger redaction).
- Prefer tokenization; persist at most last-4, brand, expiry month/year, and provider tokens.
- Validate card shape client + server (length, expiry, CVV digits, Luhn optional plus).
- HTTPS everywhere in deployed environments.

## OWASP + headers (maximize)

- Every endpoint must use the shared security-headers helper and pass the endpoint OWASP checklist (see `endpoint-owasp` rule).
- Security headers, CORS allowlist, input validation, rate limits on writes/payments, `no-store` on sensitive responses.
- Prefer validating deployed HTTPS headers with [Mozilla Observatory](https://observatory.mozilla.org/) (listed in brief references).
- Secrets in env / AWS Secrets Manager / SSM — not in git.
- Public repo: strip brand name, credentials, and internal UAT passwords from all committed files.

## Git hygiene

Ignore: `.env`, `.env.*`, `docs/fullstack-test.md` (if it contains secrets/brand), provider credential dumps. Ship `.env.example` with empty placeholders and neutral names.
